  "name": "VLDL Cholesterol",
  "code": "VLDL",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><br></p><p style=\"text-align: start\">A VLDL (very low-density lipoprotein) cholesterol test measures the amount of VLDL cholesterol in your blood. VLDL is a type of lipoprotein that carries triglycerides (a type of fat) from the liver to other parts of the body. High levels of VLDL cholesterol can increase your risk of developing heart disease.</p><table><thead><tr><th><div>VLDL Cholesterol Level</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>Less than 30 mg/dL</div></td><td><div>Normal</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>30-38 mg/dL</div></td><td><div>Borderline high</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>38 mg/dL or higher</div></td><td><div>High</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
